   <p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>
   <p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;">The Company&#8217;s effective tax rate was (<ix:nonFraction id="c108846618" contextRef="d_2022-01-01_2022-12-31" unitRef="Pure" name="us-gaap:EffectiveIncomeTaxRateContinuingOperations" scale="-2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" decimals="4" sign="-">0.19</ix:nonFraction>)% and <ix:nonFraction id="c108846619" contextRef="d_2023-01-01_2023-12-31" unitRef="Pure" name="us-gaap:EffectiveIncomeTaxRateContinuingOperations" scale="-2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" decimals="4">1.15</ix:nonFraction>% for the years-ended <em style="font: inherit;"> December 31, 2022</em> and <em style="font: inherit;"> December 31, 2023</em>, respectively. The effective tax rate for <em style="font: inherit;">2022</em> was principally due to tax expense incurred on the operation of acquired goodwill that is deductible for tax purposes and which was fully impaired for book purposes during the year. The effective tax rate for <em style="font: inherit;">2023</em> was principally&#160;due to tax expense incurred on the operations of the Company's UK business, non-deductible executive stock compensation expense, and the change in fair value of the warrant liability.</p>
   <p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>
   <p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;">The Company&#8217;s deferred tax assets and liabilities as of the dates indicated were as follows (in thousands):</p>
